{"id":"word:hebrew:H1471","type":"word","title":"גּוֹי","subtitle":"H1471 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"a foreign nation ; hence, a Gentile ; also (figuratively) a troop of animals, or a flight of locusts","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to גּוֹי (H1471) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m n-pr-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 567 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"גּוֹי (gôwy) means a foreign nation ; hence, a Gentile ; also (figuratively) a troop of animals, or a flight of locusts First listed occurrence: 1Chr 14 17."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"גּוֹי","transliteration":"gôwy","pronunciation":"go'-ee","strong":"H1471","lemmaId":"hebrew:H1471","partOfSpeech":"n-m n-pr-m","forms":["הַ/גּוֹיִ֔ם","הַ/גּוֹיִ֖ם","הַ/גּוֹיִ֑ם","הַ/גּוֹיִם֙","גּוֹיִ֔ם"],"morphs":[["HTd/Ncmpa",177],["HNcmpa",135],["HRd/Ncmpa",93],["HNcmsa",58],["HR/Ncmsa",28],["HTd/Ncmsa",27],["HNcmpc",11],["HR/Ncmpa",5],["HNp",5],["HC/Rd/Ncmpa",4]]},"definitions":{"short":"a foreign nation ; hence, a Gentile ; also (figuratively) a troop of animals, or a flight of locusts","usage":"Gentile, heathen, nation, people.","full":"H1471. goy גּוֺי 561 noun masculine Gen 12:2 nation, people (Late Hebrew id. Gentiles , Phoenician גו community , , Sabean גו id. , DHM ZMG 1883, 348 ) — ׳ג 12:2 121t.; suffix 1 singular גּוֺיִ Zeph 2:9 , גּוֺיֶ֑ךָ Psa 106:5 , גּוֺיֵךְ Kt Ezek 36:13-14 , 15 (Qr wrongly גּוֺיַיִךְ compare Co, who strike out 36:15 ); plural גּוֺיִם Gen 10:5 410t. + Qr 25:23 ; Psa 79:10 (Kt גיים ) + 6 t. Ezekiel (variant reading emended Co); construct גּוֺיֵי Gen 18:18 8 t., גּוֺיֵ 2Chr 32:13 ; Ezra 6:21 (compare Baer's notes); suffix גּוֺיֵהֶם Gen 10:5 , 20 , 31 , 32 ; &#8212; 1 nation, people Gen 10:5 (twice in verse); 10:20 , 31 , 32 (twice in verse) (all P) +; Isa 2:2 , 4 (twice in verse) = Micah 4:2-3 ,(twice in verse); Job 12:23 (twice in verse); 34:29 ; Prov 14:34 ; הָאָרֶץ גּוֺיֵי כֹּל Gen 18:18 ; 22:18 ; 26:4 (all J); Deut 28:1 . a. specifically of descendants of Abraham, גָּדוֺל גּוֺי Gen 12:2 ; compare 18:18 (both J), גּוֺיִם 17:6 , גּוֺיִם הֲמוֺן 17:4 , 15 (all P); of Sarah גּוֺיִם 17:16 (P); of Ishmael גּוֺי 21:13 , גָּדוֺל גָּוֺי 21:18 (both E), גָּדוֺל גּוֺי 17:20 (P); of Jacob גּוֺיִם וּקְהַל גּוֺי 35:11 (P), גָּדוֺל גּוֺי 46:3 (E); of Ephraim הַגּ ׳מְלֹא 48:19 (J); of Moses גָּדוֺל גּוֺי Exod 32:10 (J) compare Num 14:12 (J) Deut 9:14 ; of Jacob and Esau as two nations Gen 25:23 (J). b. definitely of Israel Exod 19:6 ( ׳גּ קָדוֺשׁ ) 33:13 (both J E), Deut 4:6 ( הַזֶּה הַגָּדוֺל הַגּוֺי , said by heathen compare 4:7 ; 4:8 ) see also 4:34 , 26:5 compare Psa 33:12 ; 83:5 (said by enemies) Jer 31:36 ; 33:24 ; Ezek 37:22 ; in narrative Josh 3:17 ; 4:1 ; 5:8 (JE), 5:6 (D), 10:13 (in poetry, no article); of Israel and Judah as two nations Ezek 35:10 (said by heathen) 37:22 ; of Judah Isa 26:2 , 15 (twice in verse); compare 58:2 ; 60:22 ; Micah 4:7 ; once my people Zeph 2:9 (|| עַם ); thy people Psa 106:5 (i.e. of ׳י ), compare also Ezek 36:13-14 , (read Kt); especially of Israel and (or) Judah as sinful, rebellious Deut 32:28 ; Judg 2:20 ; Isa 1:4 ; 10:6 ; Jer 5:9 , 29 ; 7:28 ; 9:8 ; 12:17 ; Ezek 2:3 (strike out ᵐ5 Co) Hag 2:14 ; Mal 3:9 . &#8212; Note. This definite reference to Israel and (or) Judah is comparatively rare; in Hexateuch not P (yet see Gen 17:4-5 , 6 , 16 ; 35:11 P); seldom in exile & post-exile prophets; not Chronicles — c. usually of non-Hebrew peoples Exod 9:24 ; 34:10 (JE) Lev 25:44 (H) Num 14:15 (J) Deut 15:6 (twice in verse); 1Kin 5:11 ; 1Chr 14:17 ; 16:20 ; Isa 11:10 , 12 + often; opposed to Israel as י ׳עם 2Sam 7:23 ; 1Chr 17:21 (twice in verse) etc., see עם , compare also Num 23:9 ; note especially הַגּוֺיִם גְּלִיל Isaiah 8:23 circle or district of the nations (see גָּלִיל ); also הַגּ ׳חֲרשֶׁת Judg 4:2 , 13 , 16 Charosheth of the nations , & לְגִלְגָּ֖ל גּוֺיִם מֶלֶךְ Josh 12:23 king of nations (peoples, tribes) belonging to Gilgal ( ᵐ5 Di to the district , i.e 'Galilee'); especially of these peoples as heathen: idolatrous Lev 8:24 , 28 (P) 20:23 (H) 1Kin 14:24 ; 2Kin 17:8 , 11 , 15 , 26 , 29 (twice in verse); 2Chr 28:3 ; 32:13 +, Ezra 6:21 ; Ezek 5:6 +; hostile Gen 15:14 (J) Lev 26:33 , 38 , 45 (H) Deut 4:27 ; 9:4-5 , 18:9 ; 1Chr 16:35 ; Jer 5:15 ; Ezek 4:13 +? Jeremiah Ezekiel, etc.; in simile 20:32 ; 25:8 ; sometimes || עַם Psa 33:10 ; 33:12 ; Isa 11:10 ; Jer 6:18 , see also Isa 2:2 , 4 compare with Micah 4:1 , 3 . 2 figurative of swarm of locusts Joel 1:6 ; of all species of beasts Zeph 2:14 . 3 גּוֺיִם Gen 14:1 , 9 probably mutilated proper name see below גּוֺיִם proper name, of a people Gen 14:1 , 9 , in phrase גּוֺיִם מֶלֶךְ תִּדְעָל Tid`al king of Goim ; probably a Babylonian (Elamitic, etc.) name corrupted; H. Rawlinson proposes Gutî a people northeast of Babylonia COT on 14:1 ; also KGF 258and elsewhere ; compare also Dl Pa 233 f . גול see גיל .","rootNote":"rarely (shortened) גֹּי ; apparently from the same root as 1465 (in the sense of massing);","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 14 17","keyReferences":["1Chr 14 17","1Chr 16 20","1Chr 16 20","1Chr 16 24","1Chr 16 31","1Chr 16 35","1Chr 17 21","1Chr 17 21"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":567,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 14 17","book":"1Chr","chapter":14,"verse":17,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַ/גּוֹיִֽם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ncmpa"},{"reference":"1Chr 16 20","book":"1Chr","chapter":16,"verse":20,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"מִ/גּ֣וֹי","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"1Chr 16 20","book":"1Chr","chapter":16,"verse":20,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"גּ֔וֹי","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsa"},{"reference":"1Chr 16 24","book":"1Chr","chapter":16,"verse":24,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"בַ/גּוֹיִם֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HRd/Ncmpa"},{"refere